Short:        MPEG-1 and MPEG-2 video decoder library
Author:       Brian King; libmpeg2 by Aaron Holtzman, Michel Lespinasse et al.
Uploader:     Brian King
Type:         util/libs
Version:      2.3
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Distribution: Aminet
Requires:     68020+
Replaces:     -

mpegv.library decodes MPEG-1 and MPEG-2 video by the CPU, for any
program, as mpega.library decodes MPEG audio. A 68020 or better; no FPU
needed.

- Program Streams are demultiplexed as they are read: MPEG-1's (.mpg, a
  VCD's .dat) and MPEG-2's (a DVD's .vob). The video is decoded, the
  other packets (MPEG audio; private stream 1's AC-3, DTS, LPCM and
  subpictures; navigation packets) handed to the program with their
  times. Bare video streams (.m1v, .m2v) too.
- MPEG-2 main profile 4:2:0, as on a DVD: interlaced and progressive,
  frame and field pictures, 3:2 pulldown, 4:3 and 16:9.
- Pictures in display order as the decoder's own Y, Cb and Cr planes,
  not copied, with integer 90 kHz times.
- B pictures can be passed over when the CPU is behind.
- Helpers: packed YUV 4:2:2 for a graphics card's overlay (Picasso96's
  PIP, which scales it), RGB in thirteen formats (every 15-, 16-, 24- and
  32-bit one) at its size or scaled as it is written, straight into a
  screen's bitmap, 8-bit greys for an AGA screen (WriteChunkyPixels).

The decoder is libmpeg2 0.5.1, made faster for a 68k (its IDCT and its
coefficients' decoding partly in 68k assembler): its IDCT within IEEE
1180, everything else libmpeg2's to the bit. A VCD picture (352 x 240)
takes about 10.6 million 68020 cycles, a DVD's (720 x 576) about 73
million: under Amiberry's JIT, a DVD plays at its full rate.

Version 2 is source-compatible with version 1: programs built for 1 run
unchanged.

Contents:

  mpegv/Libs/mpegv.library      copy to LIBS:
  mpegv/Include/                libraries, clib, inline and proto headers
  mpegv/mpegv.doc               the autodoc
  mpegv/mpegv_lib.sfd
  mpegv/Example/mpvplay         plays a file's pictures (RTG: in a window,
                                RGB; AGA: a screen of greys)
  mpegv/README.md, CHANGES

Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later (mpegv/LICENSE): libmpeg2 is GPL-2.0-or-later.
The includes, the sfd and the autodoc are MIT: any program may open the
library.

Source (this archive has none): https://github.com/luvwagn/mpegv.library
The source of this version is the repository's history at "mpegv 2.3",
with the example's and the tests'.

History:
2.3  MpvToRGBScaled: RGB at another size as it is written, in a screen's
     own format; every 15- and 16-bit format (555 PC, BGR 565 and 555).
2.2  Times after MPVC_FLUSH are the new stream's own: an open GOP's first
     B pictures (a DVD's, after a jump) timed back from the I picture
     after them, not carried on from before the flush.
2.1  7-9% faster: the IDCT's columns Arai, Agui and Nakajima's in 68k
     assembler (within IEEE 1180, no longer libmpeg2's to the bit), the
     coefficients decoded in 68k assembler.
2.0  libmpeg2 decodes: MPEG-2 (DVDs) as well as MPEG-1; MPEG-2 Program
     Streams (VOBs); MpvExamine, each picture's fields and duration,
     MPVC_FLUSH. Now GPL-3.0-or-later.
1.0  First release (pl_mpeg, MPEG-1). Made for AmigaMCE.
